From: Kreijstal <rainb@tfwno.gf>
Subject: [PATCH] DHT: speak the Ares 2.4.x obfuscated packet format

The released Ares 2.4.6 binary does not send the plain $E9/$EA DHT
packets built by the published dhtsocket.pas: it wraps every one of them
in an obfuscation layer (header byte $98, SHA-1 of the body, an
XTEA-like block cipher keyed from that hash, a CRC-32 and a byte stream
cipher) that is missing from the source release.  Since 15 Nov 2015
(EncodeDate(2015,11,15) < Now in the DHT thread constructor at 0x0058a25a)
the binary also drops every DHT packet that is not obfuscated, so a build
from the published sources is ignored by every Ares peer on the network.

Recovered from the 2.4.6.3072 binary (send 0x0058996c, receive 0x0058b200)
and checked against packets captured from two copies of it talking to each
other: dhtobfuscate.pas decodes them, and they decode ours.  DHT_send now
always obfuscates; udp_Receive unwraps $98 packets before dispatching them
(plain packets are still accepted).

---
diff --git a/DHT/dhtobfuscate.pas b/DHT/dhtobfuscate.pas
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e077496
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DHT/dhtobfuscate.pas
@@ -0,0 +1,298 @@
